    "details": {
      "alignment": "Lawful Good",
      "type": {
        "value": "monstrosity",
        "subtype": "Underground monster"
      },
      "cr": 2,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Asgore.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 2, power rating 8 → CR 2 as a boss. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>King of the Underground / Father of Flowey</strong> — Monster Underground Royal Family</p><p>Status: Active — authorized localized surface transport under a binding secrecy oath</p><p>Asgore is the monarch Sans names as both barrier authority and father of the dead child who became Flowey.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Royal Trident</strong> — “As a monarch, Asgore commands absolute rule over the subterranean domain, yet this authority is a heavy crown to wear; he is not merely a ruler by choice, but a guardian bound by duty.”</li><li><strong>Fire Wave</strong> — “As a monarch, Asgore commands absolute rule over the subterranean domain, yet this authority is a heavy crown to wear; he is not merely a ruler by choice, but a guardian bound by duty.”</li><li><strong>Multiattack</strong> — “As a monarch, Asgore commands absolute rule over the subterranean domain, yet this authority is a heavy crown to wear; he is not merely a ruler by choice, but a guardian bound by duty.”</li><li><strong>A Heavy Crown</strong> — “As a monarch, Asgore commands absolute rule over the subterranean domain, yet this authority is a heavy crown to wear; he is not merely a ruler by choice, but a guardian bound by duty.”</li><li><strong>Oath-Bound Transport</strong> — “Active — authorized localized surface transport under a binding secrecy oath”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/asgore</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/asgore</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
